var APPROVAL_STATE_DESCRIPTION = 'Review decision to record on an assertion that already exists, so it needs that assertion\'s `id` and is refused on a new one: write it first, then decide it, so putting a claim into force is never the same call that made it up. "approved" means it holds up, so replays start checking it and it counts as validated; "rejected" means it does not, so replays keep ignoring it; "pending" returns it to not reviewed and clears who decided it. Omit to leave the current decision alone. Approving decides what every later replay of the trace is judged against, so read the assertion and the spans it cites before deciding, and put what you checked in the justification.';
